{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions","id":53775,"title":"What I'd like to see: Crafting/Inventions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-20T00:30:39-08:00","id":53775,"title":"What I'd like to see: Crafting/Inventions","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">I have yet to find a decent RPG which doesn't just pay lip service to Crafting with minimal rules or &quot;just buy it&quot; mentality. One of the draws (for me) of Sci-fi games is the technology, all those fun toys. Whenever I made a Crafting character though, I found that most of the points I spent towards crafting turned into a waste. I was always limited by the existing list of items, weapons, vehicles, etc., that were presented in books. I figured I would write down exactly what I was looking for to keep my thoughts straight. Here are my rambling notes: </span></span><br /> <br /> Things I want for a decent Sci-fi Crafting System in an RPG<ul><li>Simple Rules with modular procedures.</li> <li>Invention/R&amp;D (Use of Tech Level?)</li> <li>Upgrades/Enhancements (optional Enchantment)</li> <li>Basic Item Creation System (Character creation system for permanent Items instead of Characters)<ul><li>Weapon Creation System</li> <li>Armor Creation System</li> <li>Tools Creation System</li> <li>Ammunition/Single Use items<ul><li>Chemical Creation System (Both Harmful &amp; Helpful)</li> <li>Explosive Creation System</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Vehicle Creation System (similar to Item Creation on a larger scale)</li> <li>Resources Gathering/Cost for Crafting</li> <li>Monetary Stat integrated into Crafting</li> <li>Bonuses for Crafting<ul><li>Workplace Mechanics (Lab/Garage/Firing Range/Etc.)</li> <li>Computer Programing Skill for automated processes (rolled as NPC when parameters are met)</li> <li>Crew Mechanics<ul><li>Assembly Crew</li> <li>Engineers/Scientists/Assistants</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Don\u2019t limit crafting potential. Offer game balance by limiting resources.<br /> Resources = physical material, Monetary, R&amp;D, and personnel.<br /> <br /> Required resources for a certain level of tech could change depending on the era the game is running in. As technology develops and new innovations are introduced (as defined by the era), the required resources could be altered to become within reach of player's abilities. This would ensure that technology too advanced for an era would remain out of reach, ensuring the themes are not derailed by rampant inventions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Idea behind the above list is to allow characters to create things. For small things, they could find the material themselves if they could not afford it. For larger things, with the proper resources, materials, assistance, etc., they would still be able to design new things. Being able to actually achieve the creation might become a story in its own right if the other players become excited about the designs the Crafter has concocted. The idea isn't to make crafting the core of the game though, just an optional mechanic that may yield rewards towards those who wish to play that sort of character.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what they plan to do for Trinity, but if nothing else, maybe this post may plant a seed that may develop into something more. Again, the notes above are my unedited ramblings, but I am curious about your opinions.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? What would you like to see in a Trinity Universe Crafting System? </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T09:10:20-08:00","id":54046,"title":"","content":"I think it could be useful to see. Certainly tech in general in Aeon needs a bit of an overhaul, perhaps crafting rules could give GM's players more scope to expand the available tech in a structured way.<br /> <br /> For what its worth, my group of Aeon players tend to just go buy stuff instead of wanting to heavily modify gear - but that tends to be just their preference for quick / less time to prep etc. They're not that big on crunch generally speaking, and my games tend to be fairly rules light though so that probably impacts things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T01:07:58-08:00","id":55317,"title":"","content":"I think the simplest way to handle crafting without resulting in pages of tables, values, materials, etc, is to have an Item Creation system much like a character creation system, only where the points spent on the item's attributes would vary depending on the appropriate crafting skill (or it's successes), but limited by the number of resources available to the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T05:50:22-08:00","id":55395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haunters</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions#post53775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">I have yet to find a decent RPG which doesn't just pay lip service to Crafting with minimal rules or &quot;just buy it&quot; mentality. One of the draws (for me) of Sci-fi games is the technology, all those fun toys. Whenever I made a Crafting character though, I found that most of the points I spent towards crafting turned into a waste. I was always limited by the existing list of items, weapons, vehicles, etc., that were presented in books. I figured I would write down exactly what I was looking for to keep my thoughts straight. Here are my rambling notes: </span></span><br /> <br /> Things I want for a decent Sci-fi Crafting System in an RPG<ul><li>Simple Rules with modular procedures.</li> <li>Invention/R&amp;D (Use of Tech Level?)</li> <li>Upgrades/Enhancements (optional Enchantment)</li> <li>Basic Item Creation System (Character creation system for permanent Items instead of Characters)<ul><li>Weapon Creation System</li> <li>Armor Creation System</li> <li>Tools Creation System</li> <li>Ammunition/Single Use items<ul><li>Chemical Creation System (Both Harmful &amp; Helpful)</li> <li>Explosive Creation System</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Vehicle Creation System (similar to Item Creation on a larger scale)</li> <li>Resources Gathering/Cost for Crafting</li> <li>Monetary Stat integrated into Crafting</li> <li>Bonuses for Crafting<ul><li>Workplace Mechanics (Lab/Garage/Firing Range/Etc.)</li> <li>Computer Programing Skill for automated processes (rolled as NPC when parameters are met)</li> <li>Crew Mechanics<ul><li>Assembly Crew</li> <li>Engineers/Scientists/Assistants</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Don\u2019t limit crafting potential. Offer game balance by limiting resources.<br /> Resources = physical material, Monetary, R&amp;D, and personnel.<br /> <br /> Required resources for a certain level of tech could change depending on the era the game is running in. As technology develops and new innovations are introduced (as defined by the era), the required resources could be altered to become within reach of player's abilities. This would ensure that technology too advanced for an era would remain out of reach, ensuring the themes are not derailed by rampant inventions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Idea behind the above list is to allow characters to create things. For small things, they could find the material themselves if they could not afford it. For larger things, with the proper resources, materials, assistance, etc., they would still be able to design new things. Being able to actually achieve the creation might become a story in its own right if the other players become excited about the designs the Crafter has concocted. The idea isn't to make crafting the core of the game though, just an optional mechanic that may yield rewards towards those who wish to play that sort of character.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what they plan to do for Trinity, but if nothing else, maybe this post may plant a seed that may develop into something more. Again, the notes above are my unedited ramblings, but I am curious about your opinions.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? What would you like to see in a Trinity Universe Crafting System? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Have you seen GURPS? That might offer insight into building your own system, for storyteller.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:37:37-08:00","id":56557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haunters</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions?p=55317#post55317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the simplest way to handle crafting without resulting in pages of tables, values, materials, etc, is to have an Item Creation system much like a character creation system, only where the points spent on the item's attributes would vary depending on the appropriate crafting skill (or it's successes), but limited by the number of resources available to the player.</div> </div> </div> </div>WW's system doesn't really strike me as 'crafting-friendly' but this is probably the way to go about it. Hmmm...<br /> <br /> The lower of your craft or resource dots gives you X points to spend. (bonuses for tools and workshops, etc.) Say I want to make an explosive, so after spending my points, it looks something like...<br /> <br /> <b>Flaws</b><br /> <br /> single-use - gives extra points.<br /> fragile - item has a single health level and dot of soak.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> compact - small and easy to carry<br /> balanced - bonus to throw<br /> <br /> <b>Qualities</b><br /> <br /> Explosive - damages multiple targets (spend extra points here for a bigger area-of-effect.)<br /> Trigger - On impact<br /> Ignition - targets must succeed on a dexterity check or be set on fire.<br /> Thrown - range based on attack roll<br /> <br /> <b>Stats</b><br /> <br /> Damage/range/Equipment bonus/etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> The result is a molotov cocktail. Remove 'fragile' and change Trigger to 'timer' and you have an incendiary grenade. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T19:39:34-08:00","id":61250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions?p=55395#post55395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have you seen GURPS? That might offer insight into building your own system, for storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect to GURPS, I think it serves better as an illustration of what <i>not</i> to do in a Storyteller system. In particular, <b>GURPS Vehicles</b> is their Magnum Opus of crafting rules, and has a distinct reputation for getting cumbersome in its pursuit of realistic results.<br /> <br /> Likewise, <b>Hero System</b>, <b>Mutants and Masterminds</b>, and <b>Mekton Zeta Plus</b> each illustrate different takes on the \u201ccharacter creation for equipment\u201d paradigm. Of the three, I personally prefer MZ+\u2019s approach the most; and if Trinity Continuum were to be set up with a \u201cbuild gear like a character\u201d system, it\u2019s the one I\u2019d recommend taking cues from.<br /> <br /> What all of these systems have in common is that they each require a full-length book devoted to laying out the standard components that are used to assemble the gear and instructions on how to assemble it. Granted, Hero System and M&amp;M piggyback off of their respective character assembly systems, which are already set up that way; but I doubt that <b>Trinity Continuum</b> will be using a character assembly system.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the issue is that all of the above systems are designed to appeal to an engineering mindset rather than a storytelling mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-22-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T20:20:03-08:00","id":73524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions?p=61250#post61250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect to GURPS, I think it serves better as an illustration of what <i>not</i> to do in a Storyteller system. In particular, <b>GURPS Vehicles</b> is their Magnum Opus of crafting rules, and has a distinct reputation for getting cumbersome in its pursuit of realistic results.<br /> <br /> Likewise, <b>Hero System</b>, <b>Mutants and Masterminds</b>, and <b>Makton Zeta Plus</b> each illustrate different takes on the \u201ccharacter creation for equipment\u201d paradigm. Of the three, I personally prefer MZ+\u2019s approach the most; and if Trinity Continuum were to be set up with a \u201cbuild gear like a character\u201d system, it\u2019s the one I\u2019d recommend taking cues from.<br /> <br /> What all of these systems have in common is that they each require a full-length book devoted to laying out the standard components that are used to assemble the gear and instructions on how to assemble it. Granted, Hero System and M&amp;M piggyback off of their respective character assembly systems, which are already set up that way; but I doubt that <b>Trinity Continuum</b> will be using a character assembly system.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the issue is that all of the above systems are designed to appeal to an engineering mindset rather than a storytelling mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen. WHile I like GURPS, Heroes, M&amp;M &amp; MZ+, sometimes there is such a thing as :Too Much.&quot; That being said, MZ+ is the better of the bunch IMHO.<br /> <br /> An Item Creation system similar to a Character Creation system, while sounding nice, would, I believe, have a lot of pitfalls. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"> It could end up a problem if the system is not balanced correctly.</span> <i>(I've rethought the following sentence, and I've changed my mind. See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions?p=77437#post77437\">This Post</a> for why I changed my mind.:<b>SCRATCH</b><span style=\"color:#008000\"> It would ultimately end up similar to building stuff in HS/GURPS, where things end up being big Point Buys, and eventually the Character becomes a distant thought.</span>)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":2141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","user":"Nadrakas","date":".  Changed one sentence. Made annotations by leaving apprpriate sentences in Blue and Green. 02-22-2014, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T12:16:03-08:00","id":77260,"title":"","content":"In my old group the way we handled gear was very rules-lite, if some piece of custom &quot;signature&quot; gear was needed and the gear fit both the chronicle and character styles and balance we just looked at similar things and determined if it was something the character would realistically have access to and if so they had it. Technical skills were usually used for repair or one-off temporary makeshift gear and continuing character background stuff (like an engineer who is called in to solve some problem which may or may not be actually something the villain is causing) and to give an idea what the PC was doing in the &quot;downtime&quot; between stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:38:21-08:00","id":77324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nadrakas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions?p=73524#post73524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Item Creation system similar to a Character Creation system, while sounding nice, would, I believe, have a lot of pitfalls. It would ultimately end up similar to building stuff in HS/GURPS, where things end up being big Point Buys, and eventually the Character becomes a distant thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, the Trinity Continuum arguably <i>does</i> need Super-Science rules, to establish what sorts of things Inspired inventors and genius Novas might create, and how they go about doing so. The trick to it is to design said rules so that they appeal to a storytelling mindset rather than an engineering one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T18:22:39-08:00","id":77437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/53775-what-i-d-like-to-see-crafting-inventions?p=77324#post77324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the Trinity Continuum arguably <i>does</i> need Super-Science rules, to establish what sorts of things Inspired inventors and genius Novas might create, and how they go about doing so. The trick to it is to design said rules so that they appeal to a storytelling mindset rather than an engineering one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely in agreement. A balance needs to be achieved in order to make such a system appealing and playable. In general there is the Freeform vs Crunch approach to Item Creation. This requires a delicate balancing act between the two, while maintaining both appeal and playability, along with keeping the system streamled and integrating the item creation process into the story <i>(if possible)</i>. Not an easy thing to do.<br /> <br /> And let me rephrase my quoted statement from above: I've rethought it, and I would like to restate &quot;<i>...It would ultimately end up...</i>&quot; and change it to &quot;<i>....It could end up...</i>&quot; -- again, depending upon how the item creation system is designed.<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N<br /> <br /> P.S.: Dataweaver: I modified the original post and changed the last sentence to reflect my change in view. Thank you for your views.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":2141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","user":"Nadrakas","date":". 02-22-2014, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}